From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Seer: settings page with auto-approve, and a first-login tour

Auto-approve becomes a switch in the Settings menu (admins), stored in the property table
and read on every request. A first-login tour highlights each feature once per user; the
done flag lives in the per-user client state, so it follows the user to every browser.
It can be shown again from the Settings page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
